# Q49 fixture: each `if`/`else` arm binds its OWN owned `String`, so the drop
# elaborator must free + Drop it inside that arm's block and never hoist the
# free to the shared exit. (A bare `puts "positive"` is a zero-copy `&String`
# borrow since the bare-literal optimization, so it would own nothing to drop;
# binding a local per arm is what exercises Q49's branch-scoped drop sinking.)
def main
  let x = 42
  if x > 0
    let s = "positive"
    puts "#{s}"
  else
    let s = "non-positive"
    puts "#{s}"
  end
end
